# Language 4: a copy with the address of the host. "hello" is written to the area 1 (the file -r) at the bit 8, 5 bytes are read back from the
# same place, stdout gets them (progs.long_rw(host_pos(1, 8), b"hello", host_pos(1, 8))). The address of the host is 2^128 + the position, the
# position is the area in the top 32 bits and the bit in the area in the low 96: 2^128 | 1 << 96 | 8 (0x1, then 32 hex digits).
:got data 40 "\xff\xff\xff\xff\xff"
:main block
:out data 40 "hello"
copy 0x100000001000000000000000000000008 &out
copy &got 0x100000001000000000000000000000008
emit &got
halt
